  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-forge",
      "text": "`dsh-plugin-forge` is a human-gated Plugin Studio for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness). It turns a plugin idea into a versioned specification, a safe project scaffold, verification evidence, an isolated DSH installation check, and—only after explicit human confirmation—a public GitHub/npm release.\n\nIt supports four v0.1 templates: `tool-command`, `skill-wrapper`, `stateful`, and `bundle`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-plugin-forge@0.1.0\n```\n\nReload the DSH Web profile. The plugin contributes `/forge` and a replayable Plugin Forge card in chat. It targets DSH `0.1.0-rc.6`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Workflow",
      "text": "```text\n/forge doctor\n/forge new dsh-my-plugin --type tool-command --title \"My plugin\" --description \"A focused DSH capability\"\n/forge continue <forge-id>\n/forge run <forge-id>          # scaffold\n\n`/forge continue` is the only way to move one workflow stage forward. Models can read status, validate, run checks, and write bounded implementation files, but cannot approve a stage, create a repository, or publish a package."
    },
    {
      "section": "Safety model",
      "text": "- Generated projects must be new directories beneath the active DSH workspace.\n- Model writes are limited to `src/`, `test/`, `schemas/`, and `docs/`; templates, dependencies, release configuration, `.git`, and credentials are protected.\n- Dependencies are compared against a small DSH/TypeScript allowlist.\n- Verification runs `npm install --ignore-scripts`, typecheck, test, build, pack preview, secret scan, and a clean DSH profile install.\n- Publishing requires the current release fingerprint. Any project change invalidates the intended release plan.\n- Forge invokes existing `git`, `gh`, and `npm` sessions but never reads or stores their credentials."
    },
    {
      "section": "Web Studio card",
      "text": "The chat card is a native DSH Conversation Node. It rebuilds status from durable `forge/*` session events, so status survives replay and loading more chat history. The card provides concise stage, check, detail, and next-command context. It uses system typography, instant progress feedback, and reduced-motion/contrast fallbacks."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run check\nnpm pack --dry-run\n```\n\nMIT licensed. [中文文档](README.zh.md)"
    }
  ],
